From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: wlroots: render/gles2: honour color encoding and range of YUV textures

The GLES2 renderer ignored wlr_render_texture_options.color_encoding and
.color_range and advertised no color encodings, so a compositor could not
offer wp_color_representation_v1 coefficients and every external YUV
dmabuf was converted with the driver default (BT.601, narrow range in
Mesa). HD video (BT.709) showed with shifted colors.

EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import carries the conversion as hints
(EGL_YUV_COLOR_SPACE_HINT_EXT, EGL_SAMPLE_RANGE_HINT_EXT) at EGLImage
creation. Pass them through wlr_egl_create_image_from_dmabuf(), remember on
the wlr_gles2_buffer which hints its image was created with, and when an
external texture is drawn with another encoding or range, create a new
image with the right hints and bind it to the buffer's texture (once per
buffer, since clients keep the representation of a buffer). Identity or
unknown encodings mean no hints (driver default), so RGB buffers are left
alone. Advertise BT.601, BT.709 and BT.2020 when GL_OES_EGL_image_external
is available.

Checked against Mesa 26.2: st/mesa takes the hints from the EGLImage into
the external sampler key (bt709/bt2020/yuv_full_range) for formats it
lowers to per-plane sampling, e.g. NV12 on Adreno 3xx (freedreno a3xx has
no native NV12 sampler).
---
--- a/subprojects/wlroots-0.20.x/include/render/egl.h
+++ b/subprojects/wlroots-0.20.x/include/render/egl.h
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
